# Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, and Docker's matcher anchors bare patterns to the
# context root (unlike .gitignore, where a bare pattern matches at any depth).
# Dependency/build-output dirs use `**/` so they stay ignored if this ever grows
# a workspace package with its own installs; `**` matches zero or more segments,
# so the root case is still covered. Everything below is root-only by intent.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results

.git
.env
.env.local
data
docs
tests
.vscode
.idea
*.log
